{"seq":1,"slug":"control-theory-basics","title":"控制理论基础","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/engineering/automation/control-theory-basics","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"feedback-and-control-concept","title":"大学自动化 — 反馈与控制的基本概念","url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/engineering/automation/control-theory-basics/feedback-and-control-concept","wordCount":1723,"readingTime":7},{"seq":2,"slug":"transfer-function-and-modeling","title":"大学自动化 — 传递函数与系统建模","url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/engineering/automation/control-theory-basics/transfer-function-and-modeling","wordCount":1661,"readingTime":7},{"seq":3,"slug":"pid-control-and-stability","title":"大学自动化 — PID 控制与系统稳定性","url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/engineering/automation/control-theory-basics/pid-control-and-stability","wordCount":1711,"readingTime":7}],"introMarkdown":"# 控制理论基础\n\n控制理论是整个自动化学科的数学内核，它回答一个根本问题：怎样设计一个系统，让它的输出自动跟踪我们设定的目标，并且又快又稳？\n\n本章从最朴素的\"反馈\"思想出发，逐步建立起传递函数、PID 控制器和稳定性分析这三块基石。你将看到为什么\"负反馈\"是工程界最伟大的发明之一，以及一个看似简单的 PID 公式如何统治了全球九成以上的工业控制回路。\n"}